e"><addressbook><name>HIBINO, SHUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANO, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIUCHI, TOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKARI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHIGE, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUETSUGU, KENICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of soldering using a lead-free solder, which comprises melting a lead-free solder which is a tin alloy containing no lead and solidifying the molten lead-free solder while applying ultrasonic vibration to at least one  of the materials to be bonded and the molten lead-free solder; and a bonded article prepared through the soldering by the method. The method leads to the formation of finer crystals of components in the lead-free solder and the inhibition of segregation of a component, which also results in the increase of bonding strength at the phase boundary of the bonding, and thus can be employed for reducing the melting point of a lead-free solder and for preventing the deterioration of bonding strength at the portion bonded by using the lead-free solder.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de soudage utilisant une brasure sans plomb lequel consiste à fusionner une brasure sans plomb laquelle est un alliage d'étain ne contenant pas de plomb, et à solidifier la brasure sans plomb fondue tout en appliquant des vibrations à ultrasons à au moins un des matériaux à lier et à la brasure sans plomb fondue; et un article lié préparé par soudage selon le procédé. Le procédé permet la formation de cristaux de constituants plus fins dans la brasure sans plomb et d'empêcher une ségrégation d'un constituant ce qui se traduit également par une augmentation de la résistance de liaison à la limite de phase de la liaison, et peut par conséquent être utilisé pour réduire le point de fusion d'une brasure sans plomb et empêcher la détérioration de la résistance de liaison au niveau de la partie liée à l'aide de la brasure sans plomb.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>